Subject: [PATCH 23/32] Retain private dashboard signing routes on the node
 hostname

---
 docs/kithmoot-node-host-ingress.md           |  7 +++-
 scripts/kithmoot-node-ingress.py             | 39 ++++++++++++++------
 scripts/qualification/kithmoot-node-nginx.py |  8 +++-
 scripts/tests/test_kithmoot_node_ingress.py  | 17 +++++----
 4 files changed, 49 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/kithmoot-node-host-ingress.md b/docs/kithmoot-node-host-ingress.md
index 4e5319b..de0602e 100644
--- a/docs/kithmoot-node-host-ingress.md
+++ b/docs/kithmoot-node-host-ingress.md
@@ -36,12 +36,15 @@ address for the dashboard's source checks. Public callers and other app gates
 cannot supply that metadata. The native header parser is bounded and discards
 addresses after validation. TURN still authenticates each admitted device.
 
-Only the node's declared HTTPS API and `/events` are forwarded. Cookies,
+Public clients reach only the node's declared HTTPS API and `/events`. Private
+clients retain the existing dashboard and signer routes on the node hostname,
+so the companion signing bridge also works in a tab or WebView. On node routes, cookies,
 dashboard bearer credentials, CSRF headers and unrelated headers are withheld;
 only a syntactically scoped Nostr authorization header passes. Set-Cookie is
 removed from responses. Unknown paths and query strings are refused. Node HTTP,
 WebSocket and stream access logs are off; native TLS errors omit participant
-addresses. This does not change normal dashboard logging.
+addresses. The original dashboard's logging is unchanged; access on the new
+node hostname is not access-logged.
 
 ## Lifecycle
 
